/* book Worked example: Q: A camera end system has three virtual links on its 100 Mbit/s port: VL1 with Lmax = 1000 bytes and BAG = 2 ms, VL2 with 200 bytes and 1 ms, and VL3 with 1518 bytes and 8 ms. (a) Find the reserved bandwidth and maximum frame rate of VL1. (b) How long does one VL1 frame occupy the wire, counting the 20 bytes of preamble and gap? (c) Find the total reserved bandwidth of the port and its load.
   1. VL1: 1000 bytes × 8 = 8000 bits; BAG = 2 ms = 0.002 s.
   2. BVL1 = 8000 ÷ 0.002 = 4 000 000 bit/s = 4 Mbit/s. Frame rate ≤ 1 ÷ 0.002 = 500 frames/s. Check: 500 × 8000 = 4 000 000 bit/s.
   3. Wire time: (1000 + 20) × 8 = 8160 bits; 8160 ÷ 100 000 000 = 81.6 µs.
   4. VL2: 200 × 8 ÷ 0.001 = 1.6 Mbit/s. VL3: 1518 × 8 ÷ 0.008 = 1.518 Mbit/s.
   5. Total: 4 + 1.6 + 1.518 = 7.118 Mbit/s. Load = 7.118 ÷ 100 = 7.1 % of the port.
   Answer:  */
