/* book Worked example 2: Q: A fibre has core index n₁ = 1.48 and cladding index n₂ = 1.46. A 50 m multimode link uses an 850 nm source launching −10 dBm, a receiver of sensitivity −28 dBm, fibre loss 3 dB/km and four connectors of 0.75 dB each. Find (a) the critical angle, (b) the NA and acceptance half-angle, (c) the link margin.
   1. Critical angle: sin θc = 1.46 ÷ 1.48 = 0.9865, so θc = 80.6° from the normal.
   2. NA = √(1.48² − 1.46²) = √(2.1904 − 2.1316) = √0.0588 = 0.2425. Acceptance half-angle = arcsin 0.2425 = 14.0°.
   3. Available budget: −10 − (−28) = 18 dB.
   4. Losses: fibre 0.050 km × 3 dB/km = 0.15 dB; connectors 4 × 0.75 = 3.0 dB; total 3.15 dB.
   5. Margin: 18 − 3.15 = 14.85 dB. The received power is −10 − 3.15 = −13.15 dBm, well above −28 dBm.
   Answer: θc = 80.6°, NA = 0.2425 (14.0° half-angle), margin 14.85 dB. In a short aircraft link the connectors, not the fibre, take most of the budget. */
