/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The system safety assessment classifies the worst effect of each function's failure, and that sets the software level.
   - Statement coverage means every line ran at least once in testing.
   - The left arm of the V goes down from system requirements to high-level software requirements (what the software must do), then to low-level requirements (the design: algorithms, data, logic), then to source code at the bottom.
   - Traceability ties the two arms together in both directions.
   - Answer.
*/
